1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,810
This tutorial explains the difference
between users and staff, and

2
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:07,239
creates a Property Manager with the right
property assignment.

3
00:00:07,239 --> 00:00:11,049
Open Settings, then Users and staff, and
check that the

4
00:00:11,049 --> 00:00:14,478
organisation above the side panel is Oasis
Crest Properties.

5
00:00:14,478 --> 00:00:17,526
Users are the people who can sign in.

6
00:00:17,526 --> 00:00:21,718
Staff Management holds employment records
such as designation, property, and salary,

7
00:00:21,718 --> 00:00:25,528
and a staff record does not give anyone a
sign-in.

8
00:00:25,528 --> 00:00:28,957
Before creating a user, search for their
email address.

9
00:00:28,957 --> 00:00:31,624
Nothing matches, so there is no duplicate.

10
00:00:31,624 --> 00:00:32,767
Select New User.

11
00:00:32,767 --> 00:00:35,434
Enter the full name, Layla Haddad, a

12
00:00:35,434 --> 00:00:38,101
unique email address, and a phone number.

13
00:00:38,101 --> 00:00:41,149
No password is set here: the new user

14
00:00:41,149 --> 00:00:44,197
receives an email invite and chooses their
own.

15
00:00:44,197 --> 00:00:48,007
For the role, choose Property Manager
rather than Company Admin.

16
00:00:48,007 --> 00:00:52,198
Always grant the lowest role that covers
the person’s real work.

17
00:00:52,198 --> 00:00:54,865
Choose the organisation, then assign the
property

18
00:00:54,865 --> 00:00:57,532
this manager runs, Oasis Crest Marina
Heights.

19
00:00:57,532 --> 00:00:58,675
Select Provision User.

20
00:00:58,675 --> 00:01:02,486
Layla Haddad appears in the list as a
Property Manager.

21
00:01:02,486 --> 00:01:05,915
Responsibilities change, so select Edit,
add a second property,

22
00:01:05,915 --> 00:01:08,963
Oasis Crest Residence Tower, and select
Update User.

23
00:01:08,963 --> 00:01:12,392
Open Oasis Crest Marina Heights under
Properties and Units.

24
00:01:12,392 --> 00:01:16,202
The overview now lists Layla Haddad as its
Property Manager.

25
00:01:16,202 --> 00:01:20,012
A Property Manager only sees the
properties assigned to them.

26
00:01:20,012 --> 00:01:23,060
Back in Users and staff, select Add Staff.

27
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:27,251
Enter the name, Khalid Rahman, an employee
ID, the designation, Maintenance

28
00:01:27,251 --> 00:01:31,061
Supervisor, the department, the monthly
salary, and the assigned property.

29
00:01:31,061 --> 00:01:32,966
New staff records start Active.

30
00:01:32,966 --> 00:01:35,633
Select Add Staff, and the record joins

31
00:01:35,633 --> 00:01:37,919
the table with the status Active.

32
00:01:37,919 --> 00:01:41,730
When someone leaves, keep the history and
remove the access.

33
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:45,921
Edit the staff record, clear Active, and
save: the status changes

34
00:01:45,921 --> 00:01:49,731
to Inactive, and the record stays for
payroll and audit.

35
00:01:49,731 --> 00:01:53,541
Then find the user, select Delete, and
confirm Delete User.

36
00:01:53,541 --> 00:01:56,208
The account can no longer sign in.

37
00:01:56,208 --> 00:01:59,256
Never share or recycle an account between
people.
